{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"length","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","reasoning_content":"We need count of satisfying assignments for CNF with 12 variables. Clauses list. Let's enumerate? 12 variables, 13 clauses. Could use brute force mentally? 2^12=4096 manageable but manual tough. Maybe use resolution? Could try to find contradictions? Let's analyze.\n\nClauses:\n1: -2 ∨ 8\n2: 6 ∨ 1\n3: -6 ∨ 7\n4: -10 ∨ 9\n5: -1 ∨ 7\n6: 12 ∨ 4\n7: 10 ∨ 3\n8: 2 ∨ 5\n9: -12 ∨ 11\n10: -5 ∨ 8\n11: -3 ∨ 9\n12: -4 ∨ 11\n13: -6 ∨ 10\n\nWe can try to find constraints. Let's denote variables.\n\nWe can attempt to find all assignments satisfying. Maybe use SAT counting via inclusion-exclusion? Might be easier to use reasoning: maybe formula is satisfiable with many assignments. Could compute using logic: treat as constraints.\n\nLet's try to see if any variable forced.\n\nClause 2: 6 ∨ 1 => at least one of 6,1 true.\n\nClause 5: -1 ∨ 7 => either 1 false or 7 true. So if 1 true then 7 must true. If 1 false, no restriction.\n\nClause 3: -6 ∨ 7 => either 6 false or 7 true. So if 6 true then 7 true. If 6 false, no restriction.\n\nThus 7 true if either 1 or 6 true. So 7 true unless both 1 and 6 false. But clause 2 requires at least one of 1 or 6 true. So at least one true, so 7 must be true. Therefore clause 5 and 3 satisfied automatically. So 7 is forced true.\n\nGood.\n\nClause 1: -2 ∨ 8 => either 2 false or 8 true.\n\nClause 10: -5 ∨ 8 => either 5 false or 8 true.\n\nClause 8: 2 ∨ 5 => at least one of 2,5 true.\n\nThus we have constraints on 2,5,8. Let's analyze.\n\nLet’s consider cases:\n\nCase A: 8 true. Then clauses 1 and 10 satisfied regardless of 2,5. Clause 8 still requires 2 or 5 true. So we need at least one of 2,5 true. So assignments where 8=true and (2=true or 5=true). 2 and 5 can be any values as long as at least one true.\n\nCase B: 8 false. Then clause 1 requires 2 false. Clause 10 requires 5 false. Clause 8 requires 2 or 5 true, but both false => unsatisfied. So 8 cannot be false. Therefore 8 must be true. Good.\n\nThus 8=true forced. Then clause 1 and 10 satisfied. Clause 8 requires 2 or 5 true. So we have 2,5 with at least one true.\n\nNow other clauses:\n\nClause 4: -10 ∨ 9 => either 10 false or 9 true.\n\nClause 7: 10 ∨ 3 => at least one of 10,3 true.\n\nClause 11: -3 ∨ 9 => either 3 false or 9 true.\n\nClause 13: -6 ∨ 10 => either 6 false or 10 true.\n\nWe know 6 may be true or"}}],"created":1790981420,"model":"C:\\Users\\d2j3\\Documents\\Codex\\2026-09-10\\napraw\\outputs\\moon-native\\models\\gpt-oss-20b-MXFP4.gguf","system_fingerprint":"b10809-5266f24da","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":768,"prompt_tokens":4200,"total_tokens":4968,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-ByYrIyscCWSDjHPxsNnOdsVk1X1CXcK2","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":4200,"prompt_ms":527.208,"prompt_per_token_ms":0.12552571428571427,"prompt_per_second":7966.495197341467,"predicted_n":768,"predicted_ms":2397.739,"predicted_per_token_ms":3.1261264667535853,"predicted_per_second":319.88469136966114}}